{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scVI n200 and multi-profile achieves ~0.65 accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 is very weak (0.21). The single image data point (config_010) leaves major uncertainty about whether the image modality can contribute meaningfully. Question: Does a stronger image encoder (ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet) produce a competitive image representation, or is the image modality fundamentally weak for this task? This experiment isolates the image-encoder variable by comparing directly to config_010 (same image-only, single-profile setup, only the encoder changes). Why this is the best next step: Before investing limited budget in complex multimodal fusion configurations (configs 028-051), we need to know whether the image branch can produce a useful signal at all. If ViT-L image-only remains weak (<0.35), multimodal fusion is unlikely to help and we should focus on refining the RNA-only pipeline. If it is competitive (>0.5), multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction. This single experiment resolves a critical uncertainty that gates many downstream decisions, making it the most information-dense use of the next budget slot."
}

